WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.700
- Hey legal eagles.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.570
Law school is really expensive,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.050
so students are always
asking me if they should work

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.360
during law school to help defray the cost.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.530
Well today we're gonna talk
about the pros and cons

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.560
of working during law school
and whether it's right for you.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.860
By the end of this video you'll know

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.470
whether you should take a job while being

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.074
a full time law student, so stick around.

00:00:19.074 --> 00:00:23.870
(soft rhythmic instrumental music)

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.240
Law school is an investment,
it has a high upfront cost,

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.610
tuition is often over
50,000 dollars per year,

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.660
plus living expenses which add in another

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.240
20 to 30,000 dollars.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.190
It's not uncommon for students to graduate

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:39.750
with over 200,000 dollars
in law school debt alone,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.710
so I understand the inclination
to work during law school

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.940
to help defray some of those costs.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.460
The question is should you
work during law school?

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.830
Is it worth it?

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.740
In my opinion, if you are
a full time law student,

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.100
no, you should not work during law school,

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.420
absolutely not, don't even think about it,

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.270
and there's several reasons for this.

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:01.580
First, law school is like
having two full time jobs

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.680
already, you go to class from 10 to three,

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.640
and then study from three to nine,

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.980
and you work weekends as well.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:11.790
Law school alone just doing the studying

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.750
and preparing for class and going to class

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:17.700
is basically like two full
time jobs back to back.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.600
It doesn't seem like
there's additional time

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.170
to factor in another full time job.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.080
On top of that law school
entails a different kind

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.360
of studying than most people are used to

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.830
and it will take you
longer to prepare for class

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.120
than you're accustomed to.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.970
You will read so much more
than you did in college

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:36.680
and unlike college you can't fake reading

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.160
the assigned reading like you did before

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.470
in your classes in undergrad.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.290
Almost all first year law students

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.300
face a very steep learning curve.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.530
You're going to have a vocabulary of words

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.960
that you've never heard
before or regular words

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.590
that have a different
meaning in the legal context,

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.910
it's a whole new set of rules.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:57.630
It's like learning
piano, guitar, and chess

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:01.450
all at the same time concurrently
in different classes.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.320
And that's why the ABA
actually puts a limit

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.770
on how much you can work in law school.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.800
The ABA says that you can
work no more than 20 hours

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.480
per week for full time law students.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.160
So they're cognizant of
the fact that you should be

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.330
focusing on law school and not other,

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.180
other monetary opportunities.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:23.260
Another factor is stress,
law school is already

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.830
considered the most stressful
time in students' lives.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.340
I've seen Marines have mental breakdowns

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.820
under the stress of law
school, so adding another job

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.950
on top of that is just
a recipe for disaster.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.690
But most importantly, the
thing about law school

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.560
is that grades matter.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.540
The most important thing that you can do

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.900
to get the job that you
want in the legal field

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.530
is to get good grades.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.730
Grades are 90% of what
it takes to get the job

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.420
that you want, whether it's a big firm job

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:55.410
or a clerkship or going
into public interest,

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.360
everyone is going to look at your grades

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.290
and better grades will
open up more opportunities.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.210
And if you take on a job
you will be competing

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.250
against students who are not working

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.540
and who are focusing on law school 100%,

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.850
and that's an unfair competition.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.370
One of the main points of law
school is to become a lawyer,

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.820
yes, but it's also to
increase your earning power

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.770
by getting into the state run monopoly,

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.350
that is the Attorney's Bar.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.400
So part of the point of becoming a lawyer

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.940
is to earn more as an attorney.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.140
So let's say that you
were somehow able to make

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.930
50,000 dollars per year
while in law school.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.310
I don't think that's very realistic

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.900
while actually being in law school,

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.300
but let's say you were able
to make 50,000 dollars,

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.380
but at the cost of slipping
a few points in your GPA.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.160
Well the difference between graduating

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.820
in the top 10% of your class
and the middle 50% or so

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.410
could result in a difference
in salary when you graduate

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.750
of 50,000 dollars less in year one.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.900
And that difference or deficit
is only going to compound

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.120
year after year after year.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.530
The place where you
start when you graduate

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.217
largely determines where
you end up five, 10,

00:04:02.217 --> 00:04:04.070
and 20 years later.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:07.130
So while it might've made
sense to earn 50,000 dollars

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:10.100
while in law school, that
could end up costing you

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.540
millions of dollars over
the course of your career.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.700
And keep in mind that
your 1L year is by far

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.650
the most important year in law school.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.760
Your 1L grades will
define where you're able

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.220
to get a 1L summer job
and those two things

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.630
will define where you're able

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.500
to get a 2L summer associate job,

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.920
and that's largely where people get their

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.770
employment prospects when
they graduate from law school.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:38.750
So if ever there was a year
not to have another job

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.320
it would be your 1L year.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.700
When you get into your 2L and 3L year

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:45.490
you'll probably get
your feet underneath you

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.750
and you can decide
whether you wanna take on

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.920
the additional risk of another job

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.300
or perhaps some
extracurricular activities.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:55.610
But your first year grades will define

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.550
whether you're able to get a clerkship

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.750
or a summer internship or
whether you're possibly

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.070
able to transfer to a better school.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:07.020
So don't short change your 1L
grades above everything else.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.110
And in fact, many schools prevent you

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.010
from doing extracurriculars
during your first year,

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.970
let alone a full time job.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:17.130
So the bottom line is
that getting another job,

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.880
especially during your 1L year,

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.840
but probably for the rest of law school,

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.530
it's just not worth it.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.250
Don't go down that road,
don't be penny wise

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.490
and pound foolish, understand law school

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.490
for the investment that it is.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.380
You're probably going to
be taking on a large amount

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:36.690
of loans and it would be
terrible to throw away

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.090
that investment just to
get a few more dollars

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.760
during the school year
which will really impact

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.480
your ability to get good grades.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.770
So in my view having a
full time job in law school

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.320
just isn't worth it.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.490
Focus on your grades,
focus on your final exams,

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.150
and do the best that you can.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:56.160
That will have the best
result in succeeding

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.990
in law school and your
career as an attorney.

